		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Glitch found in 20250323054454]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5057&amp;p=36748#p36748"><![CDATA[
You have to enter a DMR ID.<br><br>DMR won't work without an ID as its a fundamental part of the DMR protocol.<br><br>I just checked the CPS and if you leave the DMR ID empty, you get a message saying you must enter an ID.<br><br>If you start a new codeplug from scratch, the DMR ID is set to 1, however this isn't valid for networked Ham radio operation, and you may not be able to access all repeaters unless the DMR ID is in a range which they accept. <br><br>It's impossible for the CPS to cater for all possible ways that people can do the wrong thing, and I think the current message is adequate.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Apr 14, 2025 7:43 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
