		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5057&amp;p=36744#p36744"><![CDATA[
It sounds to me like it's working as intended - the APRS picks up the callsign from the call entered in the CPS, and the CPS requires a DMR ID in order to load the modified code plug with your wife's call sign into the radio.<br><br>Once your wife has her DMR ID and you enter that into the CPS I think you'll find everything works as intended.<br><br>The only potential glitch here seems to be that the CPS may not fail gracefully when no DMR ID is entered.<br><br>Cheers,<br>Mike.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4176">ZL2MGS</a> — Sun Apr 13, 2025 11:20 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
